phonometrica (0.9.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * the scripting engine has been rewritten from the ground up; this is a
    breaking change, and scripts, plugins and coding protocols written for
    earlier versions must be updated (see the "Migrating old scripts" page
    in the documentation for the full list of changes)
  * names in scripts are now resolved at compile time, so unknown functions
    and undeclared variables are reported before the first statement runs
  * new in the language: generic functions with overloads, modules, value
    and reference classes, the "is" operator, lambdas, by-reference
    parameters, list comprehensions, declarations in if/while conditions,
    separate Integer and Float types, Table and Set, and a "debug" statement
  * runtime errors now print a full backtrace in the console, the script
    editor and on the command line
  * scripts can spawn threads and exchange values through channels
  * queries now run on several threads: about 8x faster text scans and
    acoustic measurement on a 16-thread machine, with identical results;
    on by default, with the thread count and the serial threshold stored in
    the settings file (not yet exposed in the preferences dialog)
  * annotation and sound files are still read one at a time, so the first
    query of a session, which has to parse them, benefits least
  * the query editors share a single progress dialog with separate bars for
    reading files and for the work done on them
  * the statistical modeling features are now labelled as a preview
  * Phonometrica can check for a new version on startup and from the Help
    menu; the automatic check can be disabled in the preferences
  * fixed pitch measurements being read 5 ms too early; pitch values differ
    slightly from previous releases, appreciably so on moving pitch
  * fixed the same arithmetic reading outside the pitch contour for time
    points at the very start or end of a file
  * fixed preferences being silently reset when a setting contained a brace:
    the settings file is now parsed as data instead of executed as a script
  * known limitation: in the script editor, completion of names declared in
    the script being edited and live error underlining are unavailable in
    this release; built-in completion and call tips are unaffected

 -- Julien Eychenne <julien.eychenne@usherbrooke.ca>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

phonometrica (0.9.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * new "Within event" context option in all query editors: extract the
    text to the left and right of the match within the matched
    interval/instant only, without spanning neighbouring events
  * numeric property filters in the query editors now support half-open
    ranges (a <= x < b and a < x <= b), alongside the existing closed and
    open ranges
  * constraints that select an annotation layer by name now match across
    every layer whose name matches the pattern (logical OR), instead of
    only the first
  * fixed a crash in multi-constraint queries when a constraint's target
    layer is selected by name and the file has no matching layer

 -- Julien Eychenne <julien.eychenne@usherbrooke.ca>  Sat, 30 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

phonometrica (0.9.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * per-property parameter overrides for formant, pitch, and voice quality
    queries: pick a metadata property (e.g. Gender) and assign
    category-specific measurement parameters that override the global
    settings on a per-file basis; uncovered levels fall back to the global
    defaults with a one-shot warning
  * Praat raw autocorrelation is now the default pitch-tracking algorithm,
    replacing REAPER; REAPER, RAPT, SWIPE and Harvest remain selectable
  * voice quality analysis now derives pulses from the Praat pitch contour;
    a single pitch pass drives pulses, jitter, shimmer, voicing and HNR
  * short selections no longer produce 0 pulses / NaN voice-quality measures
  * scripting: reference classes are now declared "ref class T" instead of
    "class ref T", for consistency with the rest of the grammar
  * scripting: runtime errors and warnings are now reported in the console,
    rendered in red with the console tab raised automatically
  * save buttons in the query editors are now always enabled
  * macOS: fixed the exploratory-data-analysis view layout

 -- Julien Eychenne <julien.eychenne@usherbrooke.ca>  Thu, 21 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

phonometrica (0.9.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * file operations on annotations and sounds: duplicate, extract layers,
    extract slice, merge, concatenate
  * voice quality batch query (jitter, shimmer, HNR, pulse summaries)
  * mouse-wheel navigation in sound and annotation views remapped to
    pan-by-default, zoom on Ctrl/Cmd+Scroll
  * list comprehensions in the scripting engine
  * improved scripting editor: better error reporting, go to definition, auto-complete and call tips for locally defined symbols

 -- Julien Eychenne <julien.eychenne@usherbrooke.ca>  Mon, 18 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

phonometrica (0.9.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * REML estimation option for Gaussian linear mixed models, with
    model-comparison safeguards (ML/REML cross-comparison refused, REML
    comparison restricted to matching fixed-effects designs)
  * Group and Facet variables across all EDA plot types; new Pool-by and
    Style variables for scatter and formant charts; new Customize dialog
    for titles, axis labels, range overrides, and facet layout
  * improvements to the statistical engine
  * New validation suites against R-INLA (brinla reference fits) and
    against lme4/glmmTMB for REML

 -- Julien Eychenne <julien.eychenne@usherbrooke.ca>  Thu, 14 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

phonometrica (0.9.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * support for nested random effects in regression formulas
  * predicted effects and posterior predictive checks for Bayesian models
  * improved accuracy of frequentist and Bayesian regression
  * audio recording, detachable analysis plots, and per-group regression
    lines in EDA scatter plots
  * documentation now opens in the system web browser

